an>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ظهر</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">zohr</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">noon</span>","Word":"ظهر"},"id":"u_faabc_20","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ع</span>","Name":"عین","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ع</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ع‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ع‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ع</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">&#x27;</span> · a catch in the throat (a glottal stop), the sound in the middle of Cockney &quot;water&quot; — the same sound as the hamze ء. The romanisation writes it &#x27; inside or at the end of a word (ساعت sâ&#x27;at) and leaves it out at the start","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">aks</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">photograph</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">عکس</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">aks</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">photograph</span>","Word":"عکس"},"id":"u_faabc_21","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">غ</span>","Name":"غین","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">غ</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">غ‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍غ‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍غ</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">ġ</span> · like the &quot;g&quot; of got, but deeper in the throat; in Tehran the same sound as ق","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">ġazâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">food</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">غذا</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">ġazâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">food</span>","Word":"غذا"},"id":"u_faabc_22","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ف</span>","Name":"ف","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ف</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ف‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ف‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ف</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">f</span> · &quot;f&quot; as in fast","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">fardâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">tomorrow</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">فردا</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">fardâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">tomorrow</span>","Word":"فردا"},"id":"u_faabc_23","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ق</span>","Name":"قاف","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ق</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ق‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ق‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ق</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">ġ</span> · like the &quot;g&quot; of got, but deeper in the throat — in Tehran the same sound as غ, and the same ġ in the romanisation","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">ġahve</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">coffee</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">قهوه</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">ġahve</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">coffee</span>","Word":"قهوه"},"id":"u_faabc_24","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ک</span>","Name":"کاف","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ک</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ک‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ک‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ک</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">k</span> · &quot;c&quot; as in cat","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">ketâb</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">book</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">کتاب</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">ketâb</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">book</span>","Word":"کتاب"},"id":"u_faabc_25","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">گ</span>","Name":"گاف","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">گ</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">گ‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍گ‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍گ</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">g</span> · &quot;g&quot; as in gate — a letter Persian added","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">gol</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">flower</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">گل</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">gol</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">flower</span>","Word":"گل"},"id":"u_faabc_26","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ل</span>","Name":"لام","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ل</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ل‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ل‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ل</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">l</span> · &quot;l&quot; as in land","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">lab</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">lip</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">لب</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">lab</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">lip</span>","Word":"لب"},"id":"u_faabc_27","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">م</span>","Name":"میم","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">م</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">م‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍م‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍م</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">m</span> · &quot;m&quot; as in man","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">mâh</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">moon, month</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ماه</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">mâh</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">moon, month</span>","Word":"ماه"},"id":"u_faabc_28","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ن</span>","Name":"نون","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ن</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ن‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ن‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ن</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">n</span> · &quot;n&quot; as in neck","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">nân</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">bread</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">نان</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">nân</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">bread</span>","Word":"نان"},"id":"u_faabc_29","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">و</span>","Name":"واو","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">و</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍و</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">after a letter</span></span></div><div class=\"uc-sl\">never joins the letter after it</div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">v · u · o · ow</span> · &quot;v&quot; as in oven; the long vowel u, &quot;oo&quot; as in cool (دور dur); o as in story in a few words (تو to, دو do); ow, the &quot;oa&quot; of goal (چطور četowr). After خ it may be silent (خواهر xâhar)","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">vaġt</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">time</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">وقت</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">vaġt</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">time</span>","Word":"وقت"},"id":"u_faabc_30","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">خوا</span>","Name":"خوا","Shapes":"","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">xâ</span> · the silent و: in خوا the و is written and not said, so it is read xâ, never xvâ (خواستن xâstan &quot;to want&quot;, خواب xâb &quot;sleep&quot;)","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">xâhar</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">sister</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">خواهر</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">xâhar</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">sister</span>","Word":"خواهر"},"id":"u_faabc_41","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ه</span>","Name":"ه","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ه</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ه‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ه‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ه</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">h</span> · &quot;h&quot; as in hat; ح is a second letter for the same sound. At the END of a word it is usually silent and stands for a vowel (the next card)","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">havâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">air, weather</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">هوا</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">havâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">air, weather</span>","Word":"هوا"},"id":"u_faabc_31","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">‍ه</span>","Name":"ه","Shapes":"","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">e</span> · the silent ه at the END of a word: not h but the vowel e, between the vowels of bait and bet (بچه bače &quot;child&quot;, سه se &quot;three&quot;)","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">xâne</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">house</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">خانه</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">xâne</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">house</span>","Word":"خانه"},"id":"u_faabc_40","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ی</span>","Name":"ی","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ی</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">ی‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ی‍</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍ی</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">end</span></span></div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">y · i · ey</span> · &quot;y&quot; as in yard; the long vowel i, &quot;ea&quot; as in beat (سیب sib); ey, the &quot;ay&quot; of bay (کی key &quot;when&quot;)","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">yek</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">one</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">یک</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">yek</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">one</span>","Word":"یک"},"id":"u_faabc_32","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">‍ی</span>","Name":"ی","Shapes":"","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">â</span> · ی at the END of a few words from Arabic is read â, like alef","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">hattâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">even</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">حتی</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">hattâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">even</span>","Word":"حتی"},"id":"u_faabc_42","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">آ</span>","Name":"آ","Shapes":"<div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\"><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">آ</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-shape\"><span class=\"uc-sf\">‍آ</span><span class=\"uc-sl\">after a letter</span></span></div><div class=\"uc-sl\">never joins the letter after it</div>","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">â</span> · alef with the madda above: the long vowel â (&quot;o&quot; as in off, but longer) at the START of a word, where plain alef would carry a short vowel","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">âb</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">water</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">آب</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">âb</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">water</span>","Word":"آب"},"id":"u_faabc_33","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">بَ</span>","Name":"زبر","Shapes":"","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">a</span> · zebar, the stroke above: the short vowel a, as in bat; usually not written","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">bad</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">bad</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">بد</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">bad</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">bad</span>","Word":"بد"},"id":"u_faabc_34","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">بِ</span>","Name":"زیر","Shapes":"","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">e</span> · zir, the stroke below: the short vowel e, between the vowels of bait and bet; usually not written. The same unwritten e links a word to the word that describes it — the ezafe: کتابِ من ketâb-e man &quot;my book&quot;","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">del</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">heart</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">دل</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">del</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">heart</span>","Word":"دل"},"id":"u_faabc_35","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">بُ</span>","Name":"پیش","Shapes":"","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">o</span> · piš, the small و above: the short vowel o, as in story; usually not written","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">gol</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">flower</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">گل</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">gol</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">flower</span>","Word":"گل"},"id":"u_faabc_36","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">بّ</span>","Name":"تشدید","Shapes":"","Sound":"tašdid, the small w-shape above: the consonant is DOUBLED; usually not written, and the romanisation writes the letter twice","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">avval</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">first</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">اول</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">avval</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">first</span>","Word":"اول"},"id":"u_faabc_37","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">ء</span>","Name":"همزه","Shapes":"","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">&#x27; </span> · hamze: a catch in the throat, the same sound as ع; written on its own or sitting on ا, و or ی","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">so&#x27;âl</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">question</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">سؤال</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">so&#x27;âl</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">question</span>","Word":"سؤال"},"id":"u_faabc_38","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">اً</span>","Name":"تنوین","Shapes":"","Sound":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">an</span> · tanvin, the double stroke on alef: the word ends in -an with no ن written; the stroke itself is often left off (لطفا)","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">lotfan</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">please</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">لطفاً</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">lotfan</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">please</span>","Word":"لطفاً"},"id":"u_faabc_39","type":"fa-abc"},{"sub":"","fields":{"Letter":"<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">می‌روم</span>","Name":"نیم‌فاصله","Shapes":"","Sound":"the half-space (zero-width non-joiner): no sound. It ends a letter&#x27;s join without leaving a gap, between a word and a prefix or an ending written with it (می‌روم mi-ravam &quot;I go&quot;); the romanisation shows it as a hyphen","Clue":"<span class=\"uc-rm\">ân-hâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">they</span>","Example":"<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"fa\">آن‌ها</span><span class=\"uc-exr\">ân-hâ</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">they</span>","Word":"آن‌ها"},"id":"u_faabc_43","type":"fa-abc"}],"gloss":{}}